  "version": 1,
  "project": "madelon-reanalysis",
  "reason": "Three routes to compact, declared before any run toward them, for agents that run at the same time and can read this map as it changes (spec 7). Each passes screen, which rev-6 opened again, and only then differs: gradient boosting (boost), a screen kept stable across bootstrap resamples before a forest (stable-forest), and a soft vote of a forest and k-nearest neighbours (vote). screen is the milestone all three wait on, so the first agent to reach it gives the others a result to build on. The rule of rev-3 stands, and now holds by check: capture traces every command, so a captured read of data/heldout.csv before a holding resolution fails project.py check, and an agent is not shown a sibling's numbers from a run that opened it.",
